.TH CONFUSB 1 "November 2026" "confusb 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
confusb \- USB device information and driver finder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B confusb
.RB [ \-\-devices ]
.RB [ \-\-show
.IR DEV ]
.RB [ \-\-list ]
.RB [ \-\-dump
.IR DEV ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B confusb
watches the USB connections. When a device is plugged in it opens a window
(or shows a notification, depending on the settings) with all the information
the system exposes about the device and looks for its driver and the
applications needed to use it.
.PP
Without arguments it runs as a service that watches the USB connections. It is
normally started automatically with the graphical session by the systemd user
unit
.IR confusb.service .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-devices
Show the window with the connected USB devices.
.TP
.BI \-\-show " DEV"
Open the details of a device.
.I DEV
is a bus path such as
.IR 1\-5 ,
a
.I VID:PID
pair such as
.IR 058f:9540 ,
or a sysfs path.
.TP
.B \-\-list
List the USB devices and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-dump " DEV"
Print all the information of a device as text and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/confusb/ajustes.json
User settings (appearance of the cards, language and what to do when a device is
connected). They can be changed from the
.B Interface
button of the application.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The interface language is chosen in the application (language drop-down); by
default it follows the language of the desktop.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lsusb (8),
.BR udevadm (8)
.SH AUTHOR
masebastia <https://github.com/masebastia/confusb>.
